KNOWNBUG: super-class field resolution in JML expressions.

When a JML expression references a field declared in a parent
class (here, `counter` is in JmlInheritedFieldBase), the
resolver in jml_lowering.cpp looks up the field as
`<class_id>.<field_name>` only — limited to the immediate
class. The lookup fails and symex hits:

    Reason: level0: failed to find counter

The fix is in resolve_jml_expr's static-field-lookup path:
walk the class hierarchy (via class_hierarchyt or by reading
ID_super on the struct_tag_typet) and try each ancestor in
turn. The same path also unblocks fields inherited from
interfaces (Java's static fields on interfaces are inherited).

Until that lands, JML expressions that reference inherited
fields without an explicit `super.` or `this.` prefix can't be
verified.
